        {
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "propose_part_order",
            "handlerDescription": "Step 1 of 2 to order or expedite a part for a work order at your base. Pass the wo_number, a part_number from get_parts, a quantity (1-10) and priority ROUTINE or EXPEDITE. The system checks that the work order is open at your base, the part fits that aircraft type and is not already on order, works out the total and the delivery date from the lead time, and returns PROPOSED with a proposal_id, total_usd, needs_manager_approval and a summary (expires in 15 minutes), or BLOCKED with a reason_code and reason_text. needs_manager_approval = yes means the spend is above the controller's per-order limit: confirming sends it to a maintenance manager instead of ordering. Nothing happens until confirm_action is called after the controller explicitly says yes to this exact summary. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": false,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            },
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:propose_part_order_flow"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "response": {
              "type": "json",
              "value": "{}",
              "fe_metadata": "{}"
            },
            "outputSchema": "",
            "structuredContent": {}
          },
          "name": "propose_part_order_flow",
          "description": "Step 1 of 2 to order or expedite a part for a work order at your base. Pass the wo_number, a part_number from get_parts, a quantity (1-10) and priority ROUTINE or EXPEDITE. The system checks that the work order is open at your base, the part fits that aircraft type and is not already on order, works out the total and the delivery date from the lead time, and returns PROPOSED with a proposal_id, total_usd, needs_manager_approval and a summary (expires in 15 minutes), or BLOCKED with a reason_code and reason_text. needs_manager_approval = yes means the spend is above the controller's per-order limit: confirming sends it to a maintenance manager instead of ordering. Nothing happens until confirm_action is called after the controller explicitly says yes to this exact summary. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
          "schemas": {
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://propose_part_order_Args"
            },
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "propose_dispatch",
            "handlerDescription": "Step 1 of 2 to dispatch a technician to a work order at your base. Pass the wo_number and the tech_id from get_technicians (a full name also works). The system checks that the work order is open and unassigned, that the technician is at your base, holds the certification the job requires and a type rating for that aircraft, and is AVAILABLE, and returns PROPOSED with a proposal_id and a summary (expires in 15 minutes), or BLOCKED with reason_code NOT_CERTIFIED, TECH_UNAVAILABLE, WRONG_BASE, ALREADY_ASSIGNED, WO_CLOSED, TECH_NOT_FOUND or NOT_FOUND and a reason_text. Nobody is dispatched until confirm_action is called after the controller explicitly says yes. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": false,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            },
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:propose_dispatch_flow"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "response": {
              "type": "json",
              "value": "{}",
              "fe_metadata": "{}"
            },
            "outputSchema": "",
            "structuredContent": {}
          },
          "name": "propose_dispatch_flow",
          "description": "Step 1 of 2 to dispatch a technician to a work order at your base. Pass the wo_number and the tech_id from get_technicians (a full name also works). The system checks that the work order is open and unassigned, that the technician is at your base, holds the certification the job requires and a type rating for that aircraft, and is AVAILABLE, and returns PROPOSED with a proposal_id and a summary (expires in 15 minutes), or BLOCKED with reason_code NOT_CERTIFIED, TECH_UNAVAILABLE, WRONG_BASE, ALREADY_ASSIGNED, WO_CLOSED, TECH_NOT_FOUND or NOT_FOUND and a reason_text. Nobody is dispatched until confirm_action is called after the controller explicitly says yes. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
          "schemas": {
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://propose_dispatch_Args"
            },
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "confirm_action",
            "handlerDescription": "Step 2 of 2: carry out a part order or a dispatch the controller has explicitly confirmed. Pass the proposal_id from propose_part_order or propose_dispatch. The system re-checks every rule and returns EXECUTED with a reference (order PO-2026-0101 or dispatch NVA-DSP-000101), MANAGER_APPROVAL with a case_id (spend above the controller's limit: nothing is ordered until a maintenance manager approves), or BLOCKED / EXPIRED (after 15 minutes) / NOT_FOUND / ALREADY_DONE with the reason. Only call after the controller says yes to the exact proposal. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": false,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            },
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:confirm_action_flow"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "response": {
              "type": "json",
              "value": "{}",
              "fe_metadata": "{}"
            },
            "outputSchema": "",
            "structuredContent": {}
          },
          "name": "confirm_action_flow",
          "description": "Step 2 of 2: carry out a part order or a dispatch the controller has explicitly confirmed. Pass the proposal_id from propose_part_order or propose_dispatch. The system re-checks every rule and returns EXECUTED with a reference (order PO-2026-0101 or dispatch NVA-DSP-000101), MANAGER_APPROVAL with a case_id (spend above the controller's limit: nothing is ordered until a maintenance manager approves), or BLOCKED / EXPIRED (after 15 minutes) / NOT_FOUND / ALREADY_DONE with the reason. Only call after the controller says yes to the exact proposal. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
          "schemas": {
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://confirm_action_Args"
            },
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "open_service_case",
            "handlerDescription": "Hand a request that a person must decide to the right team. request_type is return_to_service (return-to-service sign-off, including closing an AOG), ad_compliance (airworthiness directive compliance), mel_deferral (deferring an item under the MEL), grounding_change (grounding or ungrounding an aircraft) or reliability_review (a repeat defect; agent_brief = the repeat-defect agent's flag). summary is a neutral 1-3 sentence summary in the controller's own words. The system routes it and returns OPENED with case_id, team and reply time, EXISTING, or BLOCKED / INVALID_TYPE with a reason. The assistant never signs off, defers, grounds or releases an aircraft and never promises or predicts the outcome. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": false,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
